1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,067
Your microwave
doesn't heat the air.

2
00:00:02,067 --> 00:00:03,633
So what's heating your food?

3
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:07,067
This part turns electricity
into microwaves —

4
00:00:07,067 --> 00:00:08,700
a kind of radio wave.

5
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:11,533
They bounce around the metal box
and into your food.

6
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:16,133
Water molecules have
positive and negative ends.

7
00:00:16,133 --> 00:00:18,167
The waves tug them
back and forth,

8
00:00:18,167 --> 00:00:19,900
billions of times a second.

9
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:22,233
All that tugging and bumping

10
00:00:22,233 --> 00:00:24,667
turns the waves'
energy into heat.

11
00:00:24,667 --> 00:00:25,800
The waves reach partway in —

12
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:28,067
heat spreads
the rest of the way.

13
00:00:29,667 --> 00:00:31,700
Some spots get stronger waves,

14
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:33,967
so the turntable
keeps food moving.

15
00:00:33,967 --> 00:00:35,600
Still — give it a stir.

16
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:38,267
Waves in, hot food out —

17
00:00:38,267 --> 00:00:40,667
and nothing radioactive
left behind.
